cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this replication package, please cite both the software/dataset entry below and the associated article."
title: "Replication package: agricultural AI, input-use efficiency and digital complements (FAOSTAT + World Bank + OpenAlex, 1961-2024)"
abstract: >-
  Code, processed data, estimation output and documentation replicating
  "Fewer inputs, not more yield: agricultural AI and its digital complements". The package builds a
  country-year measure of agricultural-AI research activity from OpenAlex (2000-2024) and
  merges it by ISO3 code and year with a FAOSTAT + World Bank panel of agricultural
  performance for 172 countries, 1961-2023. It shows that AI's measurable return appears as
  nitrogen-use-efficiency gains conditional on predetermined digital complements, not as
  yield gains.
